course: dictionary
lesson: 4542
title: Heartbroken: a very deep sadness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heartbroken is an adjective, a word that describes how someone feels. It means extremely sad, usually because someone you love has died or left, or because of a great disappointment. Look at the words around it to check.
explain: «Glum, sad, miserable and heartbroken all mean unhappy, but each a different amount.» Glum is a little sad, and heartbroken is the strongest of the four. The word tells you how deep the feeling is.
explain: Stories use heartbroken when a character's sadness is very deep, such as when a pet dies, a friend moves away, or a dream fails. You will often see it with be or by: she was heartbroken by the news.
fact: Heartbroken means extremely sad.
fact: It is usually about someone you love dying or leaving, or a great disappointment.
fact: Common phrases are be heartbroken, heartbroken by, and left heartbroken.
fact: «Glum, sad, miserable and heartbroken all mean unhappy, but each a different amount.» Heartbroken is the strongest of these.
fact: If the word sad feels too small for how a character feels, the word heartbroken may fit better.
exercise: Ben was heartbroken when his dog died. How did Ben feel? | *Extremely sad | Very hungry | Extremely excited | Slightly bored
exercise: «Glum, sad, miserable and heartbroken all mean unhappy, but each a different amount.» Which word shows the strongest sadness? | Glum | Miserable | *Heartbroken | Sad
exercise: Fill the gap: Mia was ___ when her best friend moved away. | *heartbroken | sleepy | cheerful | curious
test: What does heartbroken mean? | *Extremely sad, often because someone you love has gone | Very tired | Extremely happy | Slightly cross
test: Which sentence uses heartbroken correctly? | *Tom was heartbroken when his pet rabbit died | Heartbroken is a cloud | The sun was heartbroken | The cake was heartbroken
exam: Why would an author choose heartbroken instead of sad? | To show the character is at a party | Because it is a shorter word | Because heartbroken is a colour | *To show that the character's sadness is extremely deep
